Qoraqalpogʻiston Respublikasi Vazirlar K:
Municipal real estate properties owned by local executive authorities (excluding the city of Nukus, regional and district (city) centres, and districts of Tashkent city), with an area not exceeding 10,000 square metres, an assessed value not exceeding 5,000 base calculation units, and which have remained unsold for six months, are leased out by the Council of Ministers of the Republic of Karakalpakstan and regional and district (city) khokimiyats for a period of two years, subject to the launch of new projects in manufacturing and service sectors and the creation of new jobs, based on minimum rental rates:

    To business entities – directly for a period of ten years;

    To local or foreign specialists or organisations providing training for internationally recognised foreign language and professional qualification certificates – for a period of five years (with the possibility of subsequent extension), with no rent charged for the first year.
